From 134ce802942ecec34ecba6fafea154dd28bb6f2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:05:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] journeys viewer: the canvas PDF appends our systems, the
 architecture, the ArchiMate views and the BPMN processes, under the table's
 own names; the summary reads each answer by name

The owner (2026-11-19): "the PDF export should also append the BPMN,
architecture views. if they labeled them w/ their country systems they
should use those (they should be able to name their application
components)".

- After the sheets, the PDF has: "Our systems", every application
  component How it works lets the table mark, with its "We have it" tick
  and "Our name", as fields filled in from the same keys; the architecture
  panel, countries by layer; then a page per ArchiMate view and per
  business process (BPMN) the taught steps are carried out by. Each drawing
  is fetched as SVG, every component the table named is redrawn under its
  own name (an ArchiMate box by the element page it opens, a BPMN label by
  its words), rasterized to JPEG and embedded (ASCIIHexDecode + DCTDecode,
  so the file stays ASCII). A drawing that does not load is left out.
- The process drawings are written beside the discussion
  (discuss/figures/process-<n>.svg) for the button to fetch; the model
  carries the appendix (CanvasAppendix, pdfAppendix()).
- The lab summary names each canvas answer by its section (or card), field,
  row and column, a choice shows the option chosen (each: true) rather than
  a count, and ticks gather under their row.

Tests: 122 journeys tests pass (5 new on the appendix and the summary).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EucfRoB8Hr2JW51K9uzGtd
